# D4 "inert" companion to d4_biting.lcn: the SAME three-family structure
# (A; B|A; C|A) but WITHOUT the cross-family sentence.
#
# Its only cross-family constraint is the LMC assertion (B _||_ C | A), which
# every product joint satisfies by construction. So Credal VE with
# coupling="cross-family" gives exactly the same bounds as coupling="off" here:
# D4 is sound but inert when no cross-family SENTENCE is present.
#
# Useful as the negative control for D4 (and it mirrors examples/alarm.lcn,
# whose only cross-family constraints are likewise inert LMC assertions).
A1: 0.4 <= P(A) <= 0.6
B1: 0.1 <= P(B | A) <= 0.9
C1: 0.1 <= P(C | A) <= 0.9
